# Code optimization (strict)

## Reuse first

- Search for an existing util, hook, or component before writing a new one.
- Extract shared logic into `lib/`, `utils/`, or `hooks/` instead of duplicating it.
- Prefer the `cn()` helper (`@/lib/utils`) for conditional Tailwind class names.

## Keep it lean

- Small, single-purpose functions; prefer early returns over deep nesting.
- No dead code, unused variables, or unused imports — lint enforces `unused-imports`.
- No commented-out code blocks; delete them.
- No `console.*` except `console.warn` / `console.error`; never leave `debugger`.

## Language rules

- Use `const` / `let`, never `var` (`no-var`).
- Use `===` / `!==`, never `==` / `!=` (`eqeqeq`).
- Minimize `any` (lint warns on `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`); type things properly.
- Type component props with a `*Props` type/interface.
- Import via the `@/*` alias.

## Validation and errors

- Validate every request body / form payload at the server boundary with a Zod schema in
  `src/lib/validation.ts`. Never trust a client-supplied `documentId`, role, or HTML blob.
- Route handlers return a typed JSON error shape (`{ error: string }`) with a real status code —
  `400` for validation, `401` unauthenticated, `403` unauthorized, `404` missing.
- Surface failures to the user with a `sonner` toast; don't swallow them.

## Formatting (Prettier is the source of truth)

- No semicolons, 2-space indent, double quotes, single JSX attribute per line.
- Don't hand-format — run `yarn format:fix`.
